{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788468",
      "title": "Configuring the Custom Component",
      "lectureOrder": 15,
      "videoOrder": 12,
      "sourceHash": "78ce3f3701d7205c7256a017ca40af2f4529d165d8d26e6326ba566702538a9c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.366,
          "end": 2.1,
          "en": "- Then between those parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "we pass a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 7.166,
          "en": "just as we saw it on this app Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.2,
          "end": 12,
          "en": "And now here for our first custom Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12,
          "end": 16.066,
          "en": "the header Component, we again have to define a selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.066,
          "end": 19.433,
          "en": "that will tell Angular which elements on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.433,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "should be controlled by our own Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 25.866,
          "en": "or should be replaced by our own Component, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.7,
          "end": 31.166,
          "en": "And here the convention is to select elements by tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.166,
          "end": 34.666,
          "en": "and to select elements by a tag that consists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.666,
          "end": 39.333,
          "en": "of at least two words separated by a dash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.333,
          "end": 42,
          "en": "For example, app-header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.966,
          "end": 44.166,
          "en": "The reason for that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.166,
          "end": 46.566,
          "en": "that if you would choose just one word,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.566,
          "end": 49.833,
          "en": "you could clash with built-in elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.833,
          "end": 54.833,
          "en": "For example, there is a built-in header element in HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.866,
          "end": 56.766,
          "en": "And with that kind of Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.766,
          "end": 59.133,
          "en": "we would be overriding the default header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.133,
          "end": 61.666,
          "en": "with our own custom Component all the time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.666,
          "end": 64.2,
          "en": "and that's probably not what we want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.2,
          "end": 67.166,
          "en": "hence it should be app dash header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.166,
          "end": 71.033,
          "en": "Now this prefix here is up to you app is a common choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.033,
          "end": 73.8,
          "en": "but it could be my app, it could be your name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.8,
          "end": 76.46600000000001,
          "en": "whatever you want, I'll go for app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.4,
          "end": 80.5,
          "en": "And with that we have a selector that selects elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.5,
          "end": 84,
          "en": "that should be replaced by our header Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84,
          "end": 86.233,
          "en": "Then as I always explained before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.233,
          "end": 90.666,
          "en": "you also always need a template which defines the markup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.666,
          "end": 94.63300000000001,
          "en": "the content that should be displayed by that Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 97.5,
          "en": "Now, you could set up a template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.5,
          "end": 100.26599999999999,
          "en": "by adding a template property like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.26599999999999,
          "end": 103.5,
          "en": "and then you could set up the template as a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.5,
          "end": 108.26599999999999,
          "en": "right inside of this components. typescript file like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.366,
          "end": 112.43299999999999,
          "en": "that would work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.43299999999999,
          "end": 115.733,
          "en": "but this is actually not a recommended way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.733,
          "end": 117.43299999999999,
          "en": "of defining a template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.43299999999999,
          "end": 120.766,
          "en": "You should only use this inline approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.766,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "where you do it inside of this TypeScript file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 126.533,
          "en": "If you have super simple short templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.533,
          "end": 128.36599999999999,
          "en": "that only consist of one or two",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.36599999999999,
          "end": 130.266,
          "en": "or maybe three lines of code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 135.666,
          "en": "if you have more complex templates or simply in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.666,
          "end": 139.833,
          "en": "it is recommended that you use an external HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.833,
          "end": 144.233,
          "en": "at which you point with help of the template URL property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.233,
          "end": 146.2,
          "en": "in that configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.3,
          "end": 149.2,
          "en": "And then this wants a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.2,
          "end": 152.7,
          "en": "that contains the relative path seen relative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 154.666,
          "en": "from this TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.666,
          "end": 158.36599999999999,
          "en": "to the file that contains the markup for this Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 161.966,
          "en": "At the moment, I don't have such a file yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.966,
          "end": 164.266,
          "en": "but we can of course add one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.266,
          "end": 166.833,
          "en": "And again, the convention is to basically repeat",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.833,
          "end": 171.3,
          "en": "the name of the TypeScript file, so header.component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.3,
          "end": 173.466,
          "en": "but now since it will contain markup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.466,
          "end": 175.766,
          "en": "it should end with .html.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 179.7,
          "en": "And now you would link to that file from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.7,
          "end": 181.233,
          "en": "inside the TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.233,
          "end": 183.8,
          "en": "by defining that relative path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.8,
          "end": 186.333,
          "en": "which in this case since they're in the same folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.333,
          "end": 189.466,
          "en": "means that the path is .slash to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.466,
          "end": 190.766,
          "en": "that it's a relative path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.766,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "and then just the file name, header.component.html.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.233,
          "end": 199.433,
          "en": "With that, we can then put our markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.433,
          "end": 204,
          "en": "into this external HTML file, and here I'll for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204,
          "end": 205.833,
          "en": "use the standard header element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.833,
          "end": 208.933,
          "en": "so that's the one built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.933,
          "end": 212.53300000000002,
          "en": "It's not my custom Component or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.53300000000002,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "And then I'll just add a H one tag for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 217.1,
          "en": "with a text of easy task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.1,
          "end": 219.8,
          "en": "That could be the name of the demo app we're building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 220.666,
          "end": 224.5,
          "en": "We'll add more content to this markup later for the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.5,
          "end": 226.03300000000002,
          "en": "that's all I want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.666,
          "end": 230.5,
          "en": "Now with that, our Component is almost done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.5,
          "end": 232.8,
          "en": "but we can add more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.8,
          "end": 236.066,
          "en": "For example some styles though I'll get back to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 236.066,
          "end": 237.666,
          "en": "in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 237.666,
          "end": 240.4,
          "en": "What we should add right now already though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.4,
          "end": 244.066,
          "en": "is another important configuration property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.066,
          "end": 246,
          "en": "and that's the standalone property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 247.633,
          "en": "which should be set to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.2,
          "end": 252.233,
          "en": "Though I will say that depending on the Angular version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 252.233,
          "end": 256.066,
          "en": "you're using, this might be set to true automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.5,
          "end": 259.233,
          "en": "To be precise, if you're working in a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.233,
          "end": 262.733,
          "en": "that uses Angular 19 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.366,
          "end": 265.666,
          "en": "this will be true by default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.666,
          "end": 268.6,
          "en": "and you therefore don't need to set this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 268.83299999999997,
          "end": 269.566,
          "en": "You can omit it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.933,
          "end": 272.966,
          "en": "And you should check your package.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 272.966,
          "end": 275.933,
          "en": "to find out which Angular version you're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.933,
          "end": 277.1,
          "en": "in your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.2,
          "end": 281.466,
          "en": "Now, if you're using a version lower than 19,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 281.766,
          "end": 284.06600000000003,
          "en": "you must set this to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.06600000000003,
          "end": 286.133,
          "en": "because false would be the default there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.133,
          "end": 287.5,
          "en": "and we don't want that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 287.9,
          "end": 289.9,
          "en": "We want that to be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 290.233,
          "end": 294.3,
          "en": "Because this set to true is the modern way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.3,
          "end": 296.466,
          "en": "of building Angular components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.966,
          "end": 300.5,
          "en": "And you can use that modern way with Angular 18 as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 300.8,
          "end": 302.966,
          "en": "The rest of the component will be the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 303.2,
          "end": 305.833,
          "en": "You just need to set standalone to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.1,
          "end": 307.9,
          "en": "But with higher Angular versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.233,
          "end": 309.8,
          "en": "you don't even need to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.2,
          "end": 311.4,
          "en": "That's just important to note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 311.633,
          "end": 312.966,
          "en": "Here, I'll set it to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.966,
          "end": 315.166,
          "en": "so that it will work in either version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 315.733,
          "end": 317.4,
          "en": "Because if you're setting this to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.4,
          "end": 319.633,
          "en": "in Angular 19 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 319.866,
          "end": 321.7,
          "en": "that of course also won't be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 322,
          "end": 323.766,
          "en": "You wouldn't need to do it there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 323.933,
          "end": 326.266,
          "en": "but it of course creates no problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 326.266,
          "end": 329.33299999999997,
          "en": "if you do explicitly set it to true there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 330.266,
          "end": 332.966,
          "en": "Now, this property marks this Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 332.966,
          "end": 335.966,
          "en": "as a so-called Standalone Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 335.966,
          "end": 340.06600000000003,
          "en": "and Angular also knows other types of Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 340.06600000000003,
          "end": 342.83299999999997,
          "en": "For example, module based Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 342.83299999999997,
          "end": 346.233,
          "en": "which you would get if you set standalone to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 346.233,
          "end": 349.6,
          "en": "Now, these different Component formats exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 349.6,
          "end": 352.133,
          "en": "for historic reasons because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 352.133,
          "end": 356.33299999999997,
          "en": "in the past Angular only new module based Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 356.33299999999997,
          "end": 359.83299999999997,
          "en": "but then it introduced Standalone Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 359.83299999999997,
          "end": 360.733,
          "en": "where this is set to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 360.733,
          "end": 365.366,
          "en": "which are simply a bit easier to use and tie together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 365.366,
          "end": 367.366,
          "en": "For the moment that's all you need to know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 367.366,
          "end": 369.533,
          "en": "later I'll have a separate section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 369.533,
          "end": 372.833,
          "en": "where I dive deeper into module based Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 372.833,
          "end": 375.366,
          "en": "and the difference to Standalone Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 375.366,
          "end": 378.83299999999997,
          "en": "Since many projects out there still use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 378.83299999999997,
          "end": 381.233,
          "en": "old Component format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 381.233,
          "end": 383.933,
          "en": "it is however the recommendation nowadays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 383.933,
          "end": 386.3,
          "en": "to work with Standalone Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 386.3,
          "end": 389,
          "en": "so to set this to true and that's therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 389,
          "end": 390.6,
          "en": "what we will do here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 391.83299999999997,
          "end": 395.866,
          "en": "Well, and with that, we now prepared this header Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
